0..68 Comment "//! A value beside its code, read at each arm of a case on the code."
69..72 Comment "//!"
73..152 Comment "//! A two-code universe decodes each code to a type. A case on a code reads the"
153..232 Comment "//! goal at each arm\'s code. It also reads each later binder whose type decodes"
233..310 Comment "//! the code, so a value typed at the code\'s decode stands at the arm\'s type."
311..314 Comment "//!"
315..393 Comment "//! The case generalises its motive over the value. The kernel checks the case"
394..455 Comment "//! at that motive, and the machine runs the case as written."
456..459 Comment "//!"
460..540 Comment "//! - cites: [McBride-2002-elimination_motive] — a motive generalised over the"
541..583 Comment "//!   binders that depend on the scrutinee"
584..659 Comment "//! - see: #3483 — refinement by solution, which reads a binder after the"
660..687 Comment "//!   scrutinee at each arm"
688..691 Comment "//!"
692..808 Comment "//! [McBride-2002-elimination_motive]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-45842-5_13 \"McBride, Elimination with a Motive\""
